        "description": "<p class=\"is-style-drop-cap-with-border wp-block-paragraph\">Steve Martin\u2019s <a href=\"https://people.com/steve-martin-pink-panther-favorite-comic-scene-ever-done-exclusive-11902595\">favorite</a> comic moment of his entire career is the \u201chamburger\u201d scene from <em>The Pink Panther</em> (2006), he once told <em>People</em> magazine. Martin plays Inspector Clouseau, who has an aggressively exaggerated French accent. In the scene, he is trying to <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Z6oeAdemFZw\">learn</a> how to say, \u201cI would like to buy a hamburger,\u201d with a dialect coach. \u201cDam-buergaaaaa,\u201d he purrs at his coach, along with increasingly ridiculous permutations of all of the other words in the sentence.</p>\n<p class=\"is-style-default wp-block-paragraph\">The scene is funny because it\u2019s true for so many of us: Learning a new language as an adult can be hard. The unfamiliar sounds may get tangled up in the mouth like marbles, and the results can sound like gibberish. But for other people, ne",
